content.text:
The `user` pod is not ready for the whole abnormal window while its restart count climbs, and its resource usage is flat. I have enough to write the answer.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "attractions",
      "fault_kind": "container_cpu_saturated",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, count(*) n, avg(value) vavg, min(value) vmin, max(value) vmax FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'attractions%' AND metric IN ('container.cpu.usage','k8s.pod.cpu.usage') GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Attractions pod CPU usage jumps from about 0.002 cores in normal to about 3.6 cores (its limit) during the incident."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) n, avg(duration)/1e6 ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('HTTP /cinema','HTTP /museums','HTTP /restaurants') GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Frontend /cinema, /museums and /restaurants requests, which depend on attractions, return HTTP 500 almost immediately; attractions spans nearly vanish."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='attractions' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "Attractions emits only 1 span in the abnormal window versus about 390 in normal, so it effectively stopped serving."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "service": "user",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, count(*) n, avg(value) vavg, min(value) vmin, max(value) vmax FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'user-%' AND metric IN ('k8s.container.restarts','k8s.container.ready','k8s.pod.phase') GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "The user pod restarts 2 to 6 times and k8s.container.ready stays 0 throughout the abnormal window, versus ready=1 and zero restarts in normal."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, count(*) n, avg(value) vavg, min(value) vmin, max(value) vmax FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.deployment.available' AND service_name='user' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "The user deployment reports 0 available replicas for the whole abnormal window, versus 1 in normal."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) n, avg(duration)/1e6 ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='user.User/CheckUser' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Frontend calls to user.User/CheckUser fail with Error status in 355 of 356 spans, averaging about 0.01 ms."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "attractions", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('HTTP /cinema','HTTP /museums','HTTP /restaurants') GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Attraction-backed user endpoints on frontend return 500 errors, with the failure surfacing at the user-facing tier."}]},
    {"from": "user", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='user.User/CheckUser' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Frontend user check calls to the user service fail almost every time, so the login/user path fails for users."}]}
  ]
}
```
